// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`llmsTxt > is stable 1`] = `
"# KitchenSink

Soroban contract · 16 functions · SEP-48 · testnet
Contract ID: CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4
Explorer: https://stellar.expert/explorer/testnet/contract/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4

## Endpoints

Base: https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4
POST https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4/call/{fn}   simulate any function → { result, simulated: true, auth }
POST https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4/tx/{fn}     build unsigned XDR → { xdr, fee, auth }
POST https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4/submit      relay a signed XDR → { hash, status }
GET  https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4/openapi.json
MCP (all contracts): https://api.sonata.test/mcp — tools list_contracts, get_contract, call, build, submit
MCP (this contract): https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4/mcp

Arguments are passed by name in \`args\`. Integers ≥ 64-bit are decimal strings, bytes are 0x-hex, maps are objects keyed by the map key, enums are integers, unions are "Name" for a void case or {tag, values} otherwise, tuples are arrays, and an Option is the value or null.

\`\`\`
curl -X POST "https://api.sonata.test/c/CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABSC4/call/add" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"args":{"a":"0","b":"0"}}'
\`\`\`

## Functions

add(a: i128, b: i128) → i128
  Returns the sum of two i128 values.
bump() → u32
  Increments and returns a counter (write).
list(v: Vec<Address>) → u32
  Returns the length of the list.
ping(who: Address, n: u32) → void
  Requires \`who\` to authorize and emits Pinged.
text(s: String) → String
  Echoes a string.
maybe(v: Option<u64>) → Option<u64>
  Echoes an optional number.
tuple(t: (u32, bool)) → (u32, bool)
  Echoes a tuple.
checked(n: u32) → Result<u32, Error>
  Fails with TooBig when n > 100.
echo_map(m: Map<Symbol, i128>) → Map<Symbol, i128>
  Echoes a map.
echo_hash(h: BytesN<32>) → BytesN<32>
  Echoes a 32-byte hash.
echo_pair(p: Pair) → Pair
  Echoes a pair.
get_count() → u32  [read]
  Returns the counter (read).
echo_bytes(b: Bytes) → Bytes
  Echoes bytes.
echo_level(l: Level) → Level
  Echoes a level.
echo_shape(s: Shape) → Shape
  Echoes a shape.
echo_nested(n: Nested) → Nested
  Echoes a nested struct.

## Types

Pair (struct) · A pair of a number and an address.
Level (enum) · A level.
Shape (union) · A shape: either nothing or a boxed value.
Nested (struct) · A nested struct exercising bytes, maps and unions inside a udt.

## Errors

1 TooBig · The number was too big.
2 Forbidden · Not allowed.

## Events

Pinged(who: Address, n: u32) · Emitted by ping.
"
`;
